{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792664859151,"sessionID":"ses_e9ce51effffe4mN3wYE3w3Fzub","part":{"partID":"prt_16326f1d3001E2aCpgBwJ5Kp85","sessionID":"ses_e9ce51effffe4mN3wYE3w3Fzub","messageID":"msg_16325e96600111gT2oRcd4Dy1w","type":"tool","id":"call_00_UwbLjNpUYOQsQRwNiXI01625","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /home/baptistefaisy/aiven-kafka-demo && sed -n '150,280p' tools/emit_sql_error.py"},"output":"            from urllib.parse import urlsplit\n            parts = urlsplit(url)\n            host = parts.hostname or host\n            port = str(parts.port or port)\n            user = parts.username or user\n            password = parts.password or \"\"\n        sslmode = \"require\"\n\n    if not password:\n        raise kafkalib.ConfigError(\n            f\"mot de passe PostgreSQL introuvable (attendu dans {CREDS_ENV} \"\n            f\"ou --db-url)\")\n\n    return {\n        \"PGHOST\": host,\n        \"PGPORT\": str(port),\n        \"PGUSER\": user,\n        \"PGPASSWORD\": password,\n        \"PGDATABASE\": db,\n        \"PGSSLMODE\": sslmode,\n        \"PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT\": \"15\",\n        \"PGAPPNAME\": \"emit_sql_error\",\n    }\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# execution psql\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef psql(pg_env: Dict[str, str], sql: str, timeout: int = 45,\n         extra_env: Optional[Dict[str, str]] = None,\n         database: Optional[str] = None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env.update(pg_env)\n    if database:\n        env[\"PGDATABASE\"] = database\n    if extra_env:\n        env.update(extra_env)\n    return subprocess.run(\n        [\"psql\", \"-X\", \"-q\", \"-v\", \"VERBOSITY=verbose\", \"-f\", \"-\"],\n        input=sql, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)\n\n\ndef parse_errors(stderr: str) -> List[Dict[str, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Erreurs PostgreSQL remontees par psql (severite, sqlstate, message).\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    for severity, sqlstate, message in ERROR_RE.findall(stderr or \"\"):\n        errors.append({\n            \"severity\": severity,\n            \"sqlstate\": sqlstate or \"\",\n            \"message\": message.strip(),\n        })\n    return errors\n\n\ndef pick_error(errors: List[Dict[str, str]],\n               expected: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, str]]:\n    \"\"\"L'erreur qui porte le sqlstate attendu, sinon la derniere.\"\"\"\n    for err in errors:\n        if expected and err[\"sqlstate\"] == expected:\n            return err\n    return errors[-1] if errors else None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# sondes : chacune PROVOQUE une erreur SQL reelle\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROBES: List[Dict[str, Any]] = [\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_undefined_table\",\n        \"label\": \"relation inexistante (42P01)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_undefined_table\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42P01\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT * FROM historique_index_absent;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_undefined_function\",\n        \"label\": \"fonction inexistante (42883)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_undefined_function\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42883\",\n        \"operation\": \"historique_get\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT historique_get();\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_syntax_error\",\n        \"label\": \"erreur de syntaxe (42601)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_syntax_error\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42601\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT nom === FROM historique;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_undefined_column\",\n        \"label\": \"colonne inexistante (42703)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_undefined_column\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42703\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT resolution_privee FROM historique;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_division_by_zero\",\n        \"label\": \"division par zero (22012)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_data_exception\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"22012\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT 1/0;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_invalid_input\",\n        \"label\": \"conversion de type invalide (22P02)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_data_exception\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"22P02\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT 'abc'::integer;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_in_failed_transaction\",\n        \"label\": \"transaction abortee (25P02)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_in_failed_transaction\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"25P02\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": (\"BEGIN;\\n\"\n                \"SELECT 1/0;\\n\"\n                \"SELECT count(*) FROM historique;\\n\"\n                \"ROLLBACK;\\n\"),\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_application_guard\",\n        \"label\": \"garde-fou applicatif historique_set (P0001)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_application_exception\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"P0001\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"            from urllib.parse import urlsplit\n            parts = urlsplit(url)\n            host = parts.hostname or host\n            port = str(parts.port or port)\n            user = parts.username or user\n            password = parts.password or \"\"\n        sslmode = \"require\"\n\n    if not password:\n        raise kafkalib.ConfigError(\n            f\"mot de passe PostgreSQL introuvable (attendu dans {CREDS_ENV} \"\n            f\"ou --db-url)\")\n\n    return {\n        \"PGHOST\": host,\n        \"PGPORT\": str(port),\n        \"PGUSER\": user,\n        \"PGPASSWORD\": password,\n        \"PGDATABASE\": db,\n        \"PGSSLMODE\": sslmode,\n        \"PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT\": \"15\",\n        \"PGAPPNAME\": \"emit_sql_error\",\n    }\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# execution psql\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef psql(pg_env: Dict[str, str], sql: str, timeout: int = 45,\n         extra_env: Optional[Dict[str, str]] = None,\n         database: Optional[str] = None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env.update(pg_env)\n    if database:\n        env[\"PGDATABASE\"] = database\n    if extra_env:\n        env.update(extra_env)\n    return subprocess.run(\n        [\"psql\", \"-X\", \"-q\", \"-v\", \"VERBOSITY=verbose\", \"-f\", \"-\"],\n        input=sql, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)\n\n\ndef parse_errors(stderr: str) -> List[Dict[str, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Erreurs PostgreSQL remontees par psql (severite, sqlstate, message).\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    for severity, sqlstate, message in ERROR_RE.findall(stderr or \"\"):\n        errors.append({\n            \"severity\": severity,\n            \"sqlstate\": sqlstate or \"\",\n            \"message\": message.strip(),\n        })\n    return errors\n\n\ndef pick_error(errors: List[Dict[str, str]],\n               expected: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, str]]:\n    \"\"\"L'erreur qui porte le sqlstate attendu, sinon la derniere.\"\"\"\n    for err in errors:\n        if expected and err[\"sqlstate\"] == expected:\n            return err\n    return errors[-1] if errors else None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# sondes : chacune PROVOQUE une erreur SQL reelle\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROBES: List[Dict[str, Any]] = [\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_undefined_table\",\n        \"label\": \"relation inexistante (42P01)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_undefined_table\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42P01\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT * FROM historique_index_absent;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_undefined_function\",\n        \"label\": \"fonction inexistante (42883)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_undefined_function\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42883\",\n        \"operation\": \"historique_get\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT historique_get();\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_syntax_error\",\n        \"label\": \"erreur de syntaxe (42601)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_syntax_error\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42601\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT nom === FROM historique;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_undefined_column\",\n        \"label\": \"colonne inexistante (42703)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_undefined_column\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"42703\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT resolution_privee FROM historique;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_division_by_zero\",\n        \"label\": \"division par zero (22012)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_data_exception\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"22012\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT 1/0;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_invalid_input\",\n        \"label\": \"conversion de type invalide (22P02)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_data_exception\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"22P02\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": \"SELECT 'abc'::integer;\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_in_failed_transaction\",\n        \"label\": \"transaction abortee (25P02)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_in_failed_transaction\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"25P02\",\n        \"operation\": \"SELECT\",\n        \"sql\": (\"BEGIN;\\n\"\n                \"SELECT 1/0;\\n\"\n                \"SELECT count(*) FROM historique;\\n\"\n                \"ROLLBACK;\\n\"),\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"sql_application_guard\",\n        \"label\": \"garde-fou applicatif historique_set (P0001)\",\n        \"error_type\": \"db_application_exception\",\n        \"sqlstate\": \"P0001\",\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/baptistefaisy/aiven-kafka-demo && sed -n '150,280p' tools/emit_sql_error.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1792664859091,"end":1792664859151}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792664859155,"sessionID":"ses_e9ce51effffe4mN3wYE3w3Fzub","part":{"partID":"prt_16326f1d90015I6YTfRe0hI80w","sessionID":"ses_e9ce51effffe4mN3wYE3w3Fzub","messageID":"msg_16325e96600111gT2oRcd4Dy1w","type":"tool","id":"call_01_uDpdrgyqKKuY7bhxeFrG4651","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /home/baptistefaisy/aiven-kafka-demo && sed -n '1,150p' tools/emit_sql_error.py"},"output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"tools/emit_sql_error — publie une VRAIE erreur SQL PostgreSQL dans Kafka.\n\nComme `tools/emit_incident.py`, mais au lieu de rejouer un scenario\nsynthetique du catalogue, ce script PROVOQUE une erreur SQL reelle sur la\nbase PostgreSQL, capture le message et le `sqlstate` du serveur, et publie le\nresultat dans Kafka selon le contrat §3 (`tools/contract.py`).\n\nRegle « zero code » : `tools/kafka-incident-watch` n'est JAMAIS modifie.\nCe producteur ne touche qu'a deux choses hors de lui-meme :\n  - `routes.yaml` : une ligne par `error.type` nouveau ;\n  - rien d'autre. Le catalogue n'est pas modifie (il ne doit contenir que\n    les 5 pannes de plateforme + le run nominal, cf. `seed --self-check`).\n\nSecurite : aucune sonde n'ecrit dans la base. Les sondes qui appellent une\nfonction ecrivante (`historique_set`) echouent AVANT tout INSERT, et toutes\nles transactions sont annulees. Le nombre de lignes de `historique` est\nrelu avant et apres chaque sonde : s'il change, l'outil s'arrete en erreur.\n\nUsage :\n  ./tools/emit_sql_error.py --list\n  ./tools/emit_sql_error.py --probe sql_undefined_table\n  ./tools/emit_sql_error.py --all [--prefix P] [--dry-run] [--json]\n\nCodes de sortie : 0 ok / 1 usage / 2 configuration manquante /\n3 Kafka injoignable / 4 aucune erreur declenchee / 5 la base a change\n/ 7 generateurs d'erreurs coupes (./tools/generator on).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nPROJECT_ROOT = HERE.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n\nimport contract  # noqa: E402\nimport generator_switch  # noqa: E402\nimport kafkalib  # noqa: E402\n\nEXIT_OK = kafkalib.EXIT_OK\nEXIT_USAGE = kafkalib.EXIT_USAGE\nEXIT_CONFIG = kafkalib.EXIT_CONFIG\nEXIT_KAFKA = kafkalib.EXIT_KAFKA\nEXIT_NO_ERROR = 4\nEXIT_DATA_CHANGED = 5\n\n# --- connexion PostgreSQL -------------------------------------------------\nCREDS_ENV = Path(\"/home/baptistefaisy/hackathon-memory/.secrets/creds.env\")\nMEMORY_ENV = Path(\"/home/baptistefaisy/hackathon-memory/.env\")\nDEFAULT_HOST = \"pg-memoire-baptiste-c04f.i.aivencloud.com\"\nDEFAULT_PORT = 21492\nDEFAULT_DB = \"historique\"\nDEFAULT_USER = \"app\"\n\n# --- sqlstate -> nom de condition PostgreSQL (CONSEQUENT CONDITIONS) -------\nCONDITIONS = {\n    \"42P01\": \"undefined_table\",\n    \"42883\": \"undefined_function\",\n    \"42601\": \"syntax_error\",\n    \"42703\": \"undefined_column\",\n    \"22012\": \"division_by_zero\",\n    \"22P02\": \"invalid_text_representation\",\n    \"22023\": \"invalid_parameter_value\",\n    \"25P02\": \"in_failed_sql_transaction\",\n    \"40P01\": \"deadlock_detected\",\n    \"55P03\": \"lock_not_available\",\n    \"28P01\": \"invalid_password\",\n    \"28000\": \"invalid_authorization_specification\",\n    \"P0001\": \"raise_exception\",\n    \"53300\": \"too_many_connections\",\n    \"57014\": \"query_canceled\",\n    \"08006\": \"connection_failure\",\n    \"08003\": \"connection_does_not_exist\",\n    \"08001\": \"sqlclient_unable_to_establish_sqlconnection\",\n}\n\n# --- sqlstate -> error.type (cle de routes.yaml) ---------------------------\nSQLSTATE_TO_ERROR_TYPE = {\n    \"42P01\": \"db_undefined_table\",\n    \"42883\": \"db_undefined_function\",\n    \"42601\": \"db_syntax_error\",\n    \"42703\": \"db_undefined_column\",\n    \"22012\": \"db_data_exception\",\n    \"22P02\": \"db_data_exception\",\n    \"22023\": \"db_data_exception\",\n    \"25P02\": \"db_in_failed_transaction\",\n    \"40P01\": \"db_deadlock\",\n    \"55P03\": \"db_lock_timeout\",\n    \"28P01\": \"db_permission_denied\",\n    \"28000\": \"db_permission_denied\",\n    \"P0001\": \"db_application_exception\",\n    \"53300\": \"db_too_many_connections\",\n    \"57014\": \"db_query_canceled\",\n    \"08006\": \"db_connection_failure\",\n    \"08003\": \"db_connection_failure\",\n}\n\n# psql prefixe chaque erreur par \"psql:<stdin>:N: \" : on ne s'ancre donc pas\n# en debut de ligne.\nERROR_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\b(ERROR|FATAL|PANIC):\\s+(?:([0-9A-Z]{5}):\\s+)?([^\\n]*)\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# connexion\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef read_env_file(path: Path) -> Dict[str, str]:\n    out: Dict[str, str] = {}\n    try:\n        text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError:\n        return out\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        line = line.strip()\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\") or \"=\" not in line:\n            continue\n        key, value = line.split(\"=\", 1)\n        out[key.strip()] = value.strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef build_pg_env(db_url: Optional[str] = None) -> Dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"PGHOST/PGPORT/... pour `psql`. Le mot de passe ne sort JAMAIS.\"\"\"\n    host, port, user, password, db = DEFAULT_HOST, str(DEFAULT_PORT), DEFAULT_USER, \"\", DEFAULT_DB\n\n    if db_url:\n        from urllib.parse import parse_qsl, urlsplit\n        parts = urlsplit(db_url)\n        host = parts.hostname or host\n        port = str(parts.port or port)\n        user = parts.username or user\n        password = parts.password or password\n        db = (parts.path or \"\").lstrip(\"/\") or db\n        query = dict(parse_qsl(parts.query))\n        sslmode = query.get(\"sslmode\", \"require\")\n    else:\n        creds = read_env_file(CREDS_ENV)\n        password = creds.get(\"PGAPP\", \"\")\n        memory = read_env_file(MEMORY_ENV)\n        url = memory.get(\"DATABASE_URL\", \"\")\n        if url and not password:\n            from urllib.parse import urlsplit\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"tools/emit_sql_error — publie une VRAIE erreur SQL PostgreSQL dans Kafka.\n\nComme `tools/emit_incident.py`, mais au lieu de rejouer un scenario\nsynthetique du catalogue, ce script PROVOQUE une erreur SQL reelle sur la\nbase PostgreSQL, capture le message et le `sqlstate` du serveur, et publie le\nresultat dans Kafka selon le contrat §3 (`tools/contract.py`).\n\nRegle « zero code » : `tools/kafka-incident-watch` n'est JAMAIS modifie.\nCe producteur ne touche qu'a deux choses hors de lui-meme :\n  - `routes.yaml` : une ligne par `error.type` nouveau ;\n  - rien d'autre. Le catalogue n'est pas modifie (il ne doit contenir que\n    les 5 pannes de plateforme + le run nominal, cf. `seed --self-check`).\n\nSecurite : aucune sonde n'ecrit dans la base. Les sondes qui appellent une\nfonction ecrivante (`historique_set`) echouent AVANT tout INSERT, et toutes\nles transactions sont annulees. Le nombre de lignes de `historique` est\nrelu avant et apres chaque sonde : s'il change, l'outil s'arrete en erreur.\n\nUsage :\n  ./tools/emit_sql_error.py --list\n  ./tools/emit_sql_error.py --probe sql_undefined_table\n  ./tools/emit_sql_error.py --all [--prefix P] [--dry-run] [--json]\n\nCodes de sortie : 0 ok / 1 usage / 2 configuration manquante /\n3 Kafka injoignable / 4 aucune erreur declenchee / 5 la base a change\n/ 7 generateurs d'erreurs coupes (./tools/generator on).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Li